#!/usr/bin/python3
"""The site certificate job, run as root by portikus-certificate-job.service.

It takes the request files the admin page's Certificate tab writes into the
job directory and runs one fixed job per request: test, apply, renew,
rollback or check (docs/SPEC.md sections 21.12 and 24.8, ADR 0046). The file
contract is the comment at the top of packages/contracts/src/certificate.ts.
Caddy stays the only ACME client: this job writes Caddy's TLS snippets and
secret files, runs a throwaway Caddy to obtain certificates away from the
live site, reloads the live Caddy and reads what it serves.

Python standard library only, as the image job (ADR 0030): strict JSON
validation, atomic writes, a lock and argument-list subprocesses.

Usage:
  certificate-job            take and run pending requests (the path unit)
  certificate-job recover    mark a job the host lost as failed and put back
                             a half-applied change (ExecStopPost)
  certificate-job check      rewrite status.json, root.crt and the API's
                             trust bundle (the hourly timer)
  certificate-job reset      put Caddy's internal authority in force
                             (portikus reset-certificate)
  certificate-job first-install
                             setup's first install: read CertificateSettings
                             JSON (secrets included) on standard input and
                             write the state directory, unless it holds any
                             state already; prints changed or unchanged
  certificate-job trust-bundle
                             rebuild the API's trust bundle; prints changed
                             or unchanged and leaves restarting the API to
                             setup
"""

